# See README.md "Data & the GitHub push" — data/ is ~100MB of ATC transcript
# derived JSON that should NOT go into a public git history as-is. Nothing
# is ignored by default so `git status` shows you exactly what you're about
# to commit; uncomment before pushing once you've decided how to handle it
# (Git LFS, a private remote, or excluding data/ and outputs/ entirely).
